The README said it opens at `http://127.0.0.1:8000/console` — open that in your browser first to see the console UI.

Then test the API:

**1 — Check the server is alive:**
```bash
curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/health
```

**2 — Get a quote ID from your database:**
```bash
curl http://127.0.0.1:8000/renewal-quotes -H "X-Dev-User: officer1"
```

This returns the queue of renewal quotes. Pick a `quoteId` from the response.

**3 — Trigger an evaluation (the main test):**
```bash
curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/renewal-quotes/<quoteId>/evaluations -H "X-Dev-User: officer1"
```

This runs the full engine against your seeded customer — reads from DB, builds context, runs all 4 stages, returns the decision with recommendations.

**4 — Run the pure engine tests (no DB needed):**
```bash
pytest packages/sra_rules/tests/ packages/sra_pricing/tests/ -v
```

Start with Step 1 to confirm the server responds, then Step 2 to get a real quote ID. Share any output and I'll help you interpret the results.
